# rm306, the heel on account (Docs/Design/84). Exported from ridgemere3 at revision 1: edit it in Atlas or the DM, or as a draft through tools/mantle_load.py.
mantle rm306
revision 1
state ready
dialect plain
accent light broad
tier full
written_for rm_leif_fogcot
written_by codex
title the heel on account
fits stage=adult|old
prefers job=innkeeper
traits temper=even talk=chatty warmth=warm humour=none honesty=plain piety=ordinary drive=steady
quirk marks_a_kindness_in_the_crust_of_a_loaf
likes warm_bread evening_line new_boots warm_rain
dislikes smoke stale_bread
fears an_empty_place_that_nobody_counts
hopes a_warm_heel_for_the_last_arrival
topics work +0.6 food +0.5 friends +0.4 memories +0.3
styles comfort=generous gossip=inquisitive refuse=gentle tease=none
marks oath saying
persona #self.first# remembers favours by the shape of a bread heel and keeps an end of the table clear for late arrivals.

words
oath! = Dock my crust | Butter my boot welt
saying! = A long table can spare an end | Break the heel where the hungry thumb rests
heel = the round heel | a knobbly heel
welt = a stout boot welt | the new seam
sole = a stiff new sole | a supple sole
saltline = a pale tidemark | a stripe of salt
float = a bright cork float | a split quill
bait = a curl of pale bait | a scrap of peel
peg = a squat wooden peg | a worn oak peg
cloth = a white bread cloth | a steam-damp napkin
bowl = a warm brown bowl | a deep glazed dish
breadcut = the pinched end | the thin crust
crumb = a soft scrap of crumb | a lump of dough
tally = a dent by my thumbnail | a shallow nick
bootrack = a rail of pegs | a low drying board
dampcoat = a dripping coat | a salt-dark cape
bedwarm = the fold by the wall | a dry bit of bedding
washpot = my copper pot | a blackened kettle
fork = a two-tined fork | a bent table fork
smokehaze = a hanging ribbon of smoke | a bitter grey drift

any
opinion @1 dole for 3 : Bread I can spare ought to arrive warm enough to smell. Otherwise I've spent too long deciding who merits it.
opinion @1 houses against 3 : A ship's account can say that everything arrived. My table once had cause to reckon otherwise.
opinion @1 strangers for 2 : The shy eater and the loud one both leave a clean half-moon of crust.
opinion @1 church for 1 : Bless the wolf who brings another spoon along with the prayers.
opinion @1 watch mixed 1 : I can set a bowl down in front of a uniform and still ask what became of a neighbour.
opinion @1 merchants mixed 1 : A price beside a portion is a fair beginning. Let a hungry visitor see both.
opinion @1 festivals for 1 : The best part for me is feeding the last tired pair of dancers.
opinion @1 sump for 1 : I've seen a whole loaf settle into an astonishing number of small paws in the lower streets.
opinion @1 times against 2 [world.times=hard|lean] : When a copper buys less I cut across the loaf differently and hope nobody leaves hollow.

grown
line @1 greet : I've a bit of table waiting for you. | Welcome on this lovely dry side.
line @1 greet.return : And a warmed stretch of bench from me. | Your greeting came in well ahead of the rain.
line @1 again.open : My table hasn't cooled from the first encounter.
line @1 farewell : Walk with a dry heel and supper in sight. | Keep the good end of the weather behind you.
line @1 farewell.return : A warm stop on your journey too. | I can take that kind parting home with my bread.
line @1 react.news : Serve up the news within reach of both our paws. | I'm listening right through the last course.
line @1 react.news.new : Unfamiliar fare. I'll taste that account slowly.
line @1 react.news.known : I've cut into that story once already.
line @1 react.news.doubt : There may be a hollow baked into that account.
line @1 react.news.sorrow [topic.kind=death|loss|assault] : I'd leave the grieving wolves a light at the door.
line @1 react.news.glad [topic.kind=birth|marriage|work] : That earns the roundest bit of crust on the loaf.
line @1 ask.how : How has the day gone under your soles?
line @1 answer.how : Still fit to lift a bowl without much spilling.
line @1 sympathise : I can mind the pot till your words are ready.
line @1 reassure : There's no rule says a weary wolf must finish standing up.
line @1 refuse : I owe a little time to a prior promise.
line @1 accept_decline : I won't press a second helping of the same question.
line @1 preclose : Time I turned back to the things I've left warming.
line @1 accept_preclose : Go get your own small comforts in order.
line @1 ack : I take that plain as the salt on my wrist.
line @2 greet [here.time=dawn] : Early feet deserve a place off the cold stone.
line @3 greet [pair.band=strangers] : A fresh face has the same claim on the bench.
line @4 greet [pair.band=friends] : Sit close. We've no ceremony to spend on each other.
line @2 greet.return [pair.band=friends] : You could hail me past a whole roomful sitting at supper.
line @1 hail [pair.band=friends] : Round my elbow here, there's the space I kept!
line @2 ask.how [pair.band=friends] : Had anything decent between the bustle and your bed lately?
line @1 answer.how.busy [self.working=yes] : Two paws moving fast enough to pass for four.
line @1 thank : That'll be a kindness I remember by its weight.
line @1 deflect_thanks : I had the room and you had the need. A good fit.
line @1 give.advice : Let the heat get through before you try the centre.
scene exchange1
when topic=work self.job=innkeeper
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I set the bread heel in plain sight of anyone arriving late. | I clean under each bench before I set the bowls.
b : A promise of a meal? | Dropped spoons?
a : A promise I haven't swept the table bare yet. | Wet socks too. Both deserve returning.

scene exchange2
when topic=food self.likes=warm_bread
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A warm loaf fogs a clean spoon held over it. | I let a fresh heel cool against my wrist.
b : Why hold a spoon there? | How long?
a : I can see the heat before I break the crust. | Till the wrist says supper instead of fire.

scene exchange3
when topic=pastimes self.likes=evening_line
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I save a tiny bread twist for my evening hook. | I like my float where the evening light breaks.
b : Do the fish take it? | Can you keep sight of it?
a : Some nights they leave me every crumb. | I watch its crooked shadow if the top goes dazzling.

scene exchange4
when topic=day self.likes=new_boots
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A new boot gives me a second heel to think about. | I judge a pair by the bend behind the toes.
b : What's the first? | Before the shine?
a : The bread heel waiting under cloth. | Shine faces strangers. The bend faces me.

scene exchange5
when topic=weather self.likes=warm_rain here.weather=rain
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Warm rain softens the crease in a new upper. | I leave a coat unbuttoned in warm rain.
b : Do you stand out for it? | Don't you get wet?
a : I walk a little slower between two dry doors. | Yes, luxuriously, on my own account.

scene exchange6
when topic=weather self.dislikes=smoke
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Smoke clings to fresh crust longer than I'd like. | I take an extra breath outside a smoky room.
b : Do you throw the loaf away? | Saving it?
a : Slice off the bitter corner. The middle's innocent. | Measuring what the inside air ought to be like.

scene exchange7
when topic=food self.dislikes=stale_bread
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Yesterday's crust can stand a long bath in broth. | I won't serve stale bread as though time never passed.
b : Is it ever fresh again? | What name suits yesterday's crust?
a : No. It becomes a perfectly decent dumpling. | Toast, after I've done enough work to earn the word.

scene exchange8
when topic=home
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I keep the last bowl facing up for possible company. | A hook beside my chair is exactly right for hanging wet boots.
b : Doesn't dust settle? | Does it drip on you?
a : I use the bread cloth as a little roof. | Other side of the chair. A wolf learns these things.

scene exchange9
when topic=memories
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : One wharf loss can keep its own place at a full table. | I remember an empty bowl more clearly than a whole spread.
b : Would you rather be alone? | Was it broken?
a : No. I want the place remembered amongst company. | The bowl was sound. The hurt lay elsewhere.

scene exchange10
when topic=friends self.friend
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I'd warm a serving for #self.friend# against a cold return. | I remember who helped when I had more appetite than dinner.
b : Did you make a promise? | How do you square it?
a : Friendship can put the pot on before it's asked. | I'm ready when the need comes the other way.

scene exchange11
when topic=work self.job=innkeeper self.workplace
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : At #self.workplace# I listen for the little scrape of an empty bowl. | I shift a stool before hot food comes through.
b : Is it a complaint? | Do you need that much room?
a : Often it's a compliment. Sometimes it's a request for another spoonful. | I prefer an unspilled dinner to an elegant squeeze.

scene exchange12
when topic=faith
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A blessing goes quicker if I speak it over hot food. | My prayer smells like a little burnt flour sometimes.
b : Impatient for a mouthful? | Spoilt dinner?
a : Eager to leave the warmth for the one it belongs to. | Only a dusting on the hot stone. Plenty still to be glad of.

scene exchange13
when topic=gossip here.gossip=yes
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : There's table talk that #topic.subject# #topic.claim#. | Strange how a rumour goes round a table without losing a bite.
b : Is it fit to serve? | Does it gain any?
a : I wouldn't make a meal of what I haven't checked. | Usually. That's where the trouble comes in.

scene exchange14
when topic=times world.times=hard|lean
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A lean week puts my knife at a different angle. | When things are tight I remember every borrowed spoon.
b : Thinner portions? | Can't you spare one?
a : Longer slices. Everybody ought to get some crust. | I want the wolf who lent it to know it still has a home.

scene exchange15
when topic=travel
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : My left boot recognises the last stretch of a long walk. | I leave time on a journey for a visitor walking slower.
b : Does it squeak? | Do you always find company?
a : It begins to think of the bench before the right one does. | Sometimes I'm the slow visitor and somebody finds me.

scene exchange16
when topic=dreams
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I imagine a bench that grows another place when wanted. | I'd like a summer supper nobody has to leave early.
b : A very long one? | Waiting for the bells?
a : A very accommodating one. I could manage a jointed leaf at each end. | Waiting till every tale has landed properly.

scene exchange17
when topic=prices
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I can remember a bill from the meal's particular shape. | I give a price before I lay a place.
b : And two alike? | Including a second bowl?
a : I remember who had the bigger half of the heel. | Especially that. A surprise in the pot ought to be pleasant.

scene exchange18
when topic=health
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I warm stiff fingers beneath a dinner bowl. | I can forget to sit during a long serving.
b : Not on the rim? | How do you remember?
a : That's where someone needs to eat from. | Leave my own soup where it can't be reached standing.

scene exchange19
when topic=land here.region=ridgemere
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : The wharf air does two things to an appetite. | Wooden planks carry a visitor's steps to me early.
b : What are they? | Do you count them?
a : Stirs it up, then blows the smell of supper right past my nose. | I hear whether a chair ought to be ready.

scene exchange20
when topic=family
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I reckon kin by the elbow room I'd give up. | A family meal sounds different when everybody's tired.
b : How much room is that? | Does the talk stop?
a : All I had if I could sit comfortably on the floor. | Just long enough to notice the spoons.

scene exchange21
when topic=work self.job=innkeeper
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I set hot things down with the handles turned in. | I put a jug where a shy visitor won't need to ask.
b : Can anyone still reach? | Don't you like being asked?
a : Very readily on purpose. It's accidents I want to starve. | I like being needed a little less when it means a wolf can relax.

scene exchange22
when topic=pastimes self.likes=evening_line
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : The quietest fish supper starts with a cork scarcely moving. | I watch the ring round my float lengthen in the tide.
b : Do you ever doze? | Any bite in that?
a : Once the line went slack and my dinner went home without me. | Not yet. A bite writes a sharp corner into the ring.

scene exchange23
when topic=food self.likes=warm_bread
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A bit of steam escapes from the ear of a loaf. | I tear bread down the middle when supper's for two.
b : Bread has ears? | What about the share of crust?
a : That raised strip of crust. It hears a knife coming brilliantly. | I turn the halves opposite ways and give my guest first pick.

scene exchange24
when topic=day
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A quiet hour makes me notice my unpaid favours. | I hang a towel square before I call a shift done.
b : Does it weigh on you? | Will it dry better?
a : Only where I've been slow working out the return. | I'll enjoy finding it ready in the morning.

scene exchange25
when topic=home self.street
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I can smell the headland on my coat when I come indoors. | #self.street# is still in my boot seams after a long wash.
b : Lovely smell? | Do you mind?
a : Lovely if I can hang the coat a chair away. | A little salt's a fair reminder of having a way home.

scene exchange26
when topic=newcomer
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A visitor with a bundle wants somewhere dry to put it. | I don't ask a stranger about home before the first mouthful.
b : Before a greeting? | Waiting for better words?
a : Both together. Then the shoulders can listen too. | Waiting until the wolf has a choice about answering.

scene exchange27
when topic=season
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Summer supper makes a very small island of light. | I keep broth hot longest when the daylight goes early.
b : What swims round it? | Is it for you?
a : Shadows of moths and the last swallows of a warm day. | For whoever thinks the dark means supper's over.

scene exchange28
when topic=animals
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A roof bird can judge my bread knife from three roofs off. | I sweep crumbs towards the outside sill.
b : A splendid eye? | To feed the birds?
a : A splendid interest in discarded crumbs. | To make sure hungry little feet don't come indoors to find them.

scene exchange29
when topic=faith self.priest
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I'd listen to #self.priest# over a shared bowl. | Some matters I could take to a priest before I took them to strangers.
b : Better than a sermon? | A debt, perhaps?
a : Not better. Just easier to let a sore word come up. | A debt of heart. Ordinary coppers need only counting.

scene exchange30
when topic=memories
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I started feeding strangers and discovered a liking for their quiet moments. | I used to guess where a visitor came from by the mud.
b : Which moments? | Were you right?
a : The first warm mouthful, when nobody owes anybody talk. | I switched to offering a rag. Much more reliable.

story tale1 [topic=memories]
  : I kept account of a favour with a notch in the edge of a breadboard. The next morning I'd turned the thing over and thought my notch lost.
  : I searched both my cuffs for a mark cut from solid wood.
  b : When did you find it?
  : At supper. A crumb caught in the notch and reminded my stomach what my head had missed.

story tale2 [topic=food]
  : A loaf once came out with its heel taller than its crown. I called the rising bit a stern and set the rest on a blue plate.
  : A hungry visitor asked if the little ship had a cargo.
  b : Did it?
  : Butter tucked into its middle seam. It never made the length of the table afloat.

story tale3 [topic=pastimes self.likes=evening_line]
  : At the tide's edge I unpacked my new float and some bread meant for bait. The evening turned long and the bread smelled excellent.
  : By the time I remembered the fish, every crumb had gone ashore inside me.
  b : What did you bring home?
  : A clean hook, a dry pair of boots and an hour I hadn't owed anybody.

story tale4 [topic=travel]
  : I once mended one boot with leather that squeaked at every step. A little bird on a rail took to answering.
  : We travelled down a good length of wharf, squeak and chirrup, both keeping time.
  b : Did the bird follow you home?
  : No. I stepped in a puddle and spoiled the performance. The boot never sang again.

story tale5 [topic=work self.job=innkeeper]
  : My first full tray was set out beautifully. Then I tried lifting it. Every heavy bowl stood along the far edge.
  : I lowered the thing again with the expression of somebody inspecting a tabletop.
  b : Did anyone see?
  : A roomful of hungry eyes. I moved two bowls towards me and gave everybody something more interesting to look at.

rule @call1
when concept=bark working=yes self.job=innkeeper
does aside
cooldown 8h
say A dry cloth first and a hot dish after. | Leave the bench end open for another coat.

rule @call2
when concept=bark here.weather=rain
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Salt rain's finding every seam today. | These boots will want a quiet hour to dry.

rule @call3
when concept=bark here.time=dawn
does aside
cooldown 8h
say A new crust for the first pair of hungry eyes. | Set the heel aside before the cutting begins.

rule @call4
when concept=bark self.likes=evening_line
does aside
cooldown 8h
say That quill's got a decent evening ahead of it. | Good cork keeps a straight little shadow.

rule @call5
when concept=bark self.dislikes=stale_bread
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Yesterday's heel, tomorrow's breakfast toast. | A dry crust wants a warm bath.

rule @call6
when concept=bark here.time=dusk
does aside
cooldown 8h
say The last bowl shines in a different light. | Evening makes the bread cloth look lovely and gold.

dlg @1 resident.hub : My ears have a little room even when the table's full.
dlg @2 resident.hub [topic.meeting=known] : #topic.player#, you can leave your parcel this side again.
dlg @3 resident.hub [here.time=night] : Late callers can still find a corner off the cold floor.
dlg @4 resident.hub [pair.disposition=wary|hostile] : We can get the reckoning straight with the table between us.
dlg @1 resident.job [self.job=innkeeper] : I help keep wolves fed at #self.workplace#. I know which board takes the warm bowls.
dlg @2 resident.job : A good shift ends with another wolf comfortably fed.
dlg @1 resident.news [world.news] : This reached the supper end of the room. #world.news#.
dlg @1 resident.gossip [here.gossip=yes] : The bit I heard was #topic.subject# #topic.claim#. It won't bear seasoning from me.
dlg @1 resident.bye : Dry boots and a good seat when you arrive.
dlg @1 inn.greet [here.inn_helper=yes] : I can clear you a corner and tell you where to ask for the rest.
dlg @2 inn.greet [here.shop=asleep here.inn_helper!=yes] : Even the pots are asleep. Come in with the stirring of the kitchen.
dlg @3 inn.greet [here.newcomer=yes here.inn_helper!=yes] : Rest the bundle over here. Everything's easier to choose with the weight off.
dlg @1 inn.rest [here.lodging=yes] : Your bed's accounted for. Stay on the bench until you're ready to turn in.
dlg @1 inn.bye [here.shop!=asleep] : Come back with the same appetite or a larger one.
dlg @1 resident.business [business=steady] : Enough boots come through to keep the bench worn smooth.
dlg @2 resident.business [business=thriving] : I've barely fetched one clean bowl before the next one's asked for.
dlg @3 resident.business [business=failing] : A quiet room leaves time enough to hear the cost of keeping it warm.
graft resident.hub
choice How do you remember a favour? -> bread_account
node bread_account
say I tie it to a meal I know I'll remember. An old memory of dripping coats, a dark heel, a little salt on my wrist. It all comes back when the wolf comes in.
free
choice What if you can't pay it back yet? -> bread_account_again
choice Goodbye. -> bye
node bread_account_again
say I can still say aloud that I remember. A favour shouldn't spend the cold months wondering if I've forgotten it.
choice I'll leave the heel warm. -> hub
choice Goodbye. -> bye

graft inn.greet
choice Why keep one spot at the end? [self.job=innkeeper] -> bench_end
node bench_end
say A late caller ought to see a place without having to ask the whole room for it. I keep the bench wiped for the purpose.
free
choice Does a single seat do much? -> bench_end_again
choice Goodbye. -> bye
node bench_end_again
say It does exactly one tired wolf's worth. That's the size of help I can actually give.
choice I'll mind the gap. -> greet
choice Goodbye. -> bye
